label version_08:

    narrator "\[ VERSION 0.8 - Crunch \]"
    pause 0.5
    narrator "The commits get worse. You can feel the exhaustion in the world itself."

    narrator "Tuesday happens twice. Different weather. Same date. Nobody notices."

    narrator "Two bakeries on the same street. Identical. You work in both somehow."
    narrator "You don't remember crossing the street."

    narrator "The mayor starts speaking like someone else. Same voice, different words."
    narrator "He talks about his wife — the one who doesn't exist anymore. He doesn't know he's doing it."

    mayor "Clara always said the morning light here was something special."
    narrator "He stops. Blinks."
    mayor "I've always loved the morning light here."
    narrator "He walks away. You write Clara in your notebook. The ink stays this time."

    narrator "Then the commit messages start."

    mina "Merge conflict."
    narrator "She's standing in the bakery doorway. But it isn't her."
    narrator "Her face, her voice. The eyes are wrong."
    mina "Fixed memory leak."
    narrator "She blinks."
    mina "Temporary solution - will address in next build."
    narrator "She walks away. You follow. She turns a corner. She's gone."

    $ notebook_entries.append("Clara. The mayor's wife. Her name was Clara.")
    $ notebook_entries.append("Mina appeared in the bakery. Said commit messages. Eyes were wrong.")
    $ show_notebook_icon = True

    jump version_09
